      "WebhookAck": {
        "description": "The result of ingesting a provider webhook.\n\n`duplicate` is true when the `provider_event_id` was already in the inbox \u2014 the callback was a\nre-delivery and did nothing the first time did not already do. `reconciled` is true when the\nevent moved a charge to a terminal state and emitted a `commerce.payment.*`.\n\n`provider_event_id` is the id the inbox deduplicated on: the delivery's `X-Razorpay-Event-Id`\nheader, else an id the body carried, else `derived:<sha256>` from the body's event name, entity\nid and timestamp. It is never empty.\n\n`ignored_reason` is set when the webhook was authentic but cannot be reconciled and never will\nbe \u2014 the provider is answered 200 (a retry could not change the outcome) and the reason is a\nstable code: `unknown_charge` and `unattributable` (nothing here to reconcile), or\n`illegal_transition`, `amount_mismatch`, `currency_mismatch` and `provider_id_conflict` (it\ncontradicts what this platform holds; no state was changed, an operator should look). Every\nreason except `unattributable` \u2014 which has no tenant to record under \u2014 is kept on the inbox\nrow and audited as `payment.webhook.ignored`. Null on a webhook that was reconciled or was\nsimply a redelivery.",
        "properties": {
          "duplicate": {
            "title": "Duplicate",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "ignored_reason": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Ignored Reason"
          },
          "provider_event_id": {
            "title": "Provider Event Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "received": {
            "title": "Received",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "reconciled": {
            "title": "Reconciled",
            "type": "boolean"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "received",
          "provider_event_id",
          "duplicate",
          "reconciled"
        ],
        "title": "WebhookAck",
        "type": "object"
      }
    }
  },
  "info": {
    "description": "The provider-facing edge of commerce: mandates, charges, refunds and the webhook inbox. Razorpay-first, with the provider seam isolated so no other service knows which processor took the money \u2014 only that a charge was captured or failed. A failed charge is what suspends a subscription and, in turn, de-entitles a product (ADR-0004 \u00a75).",
    "title": "Payment service",
    "version": "0.1.0"
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/api/v1/payment/checkouts": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Open the provider's hosted checkout for one invoice. The amount is the invoice's own\ncharge's, never the body's; a second request for an invoice with an open checkout returns that\ncheckout (at the provider it was created under). **404** if the organization has no charge for\nthe invoice, **409** if it is already paid (`invoice_already_paid`) or cannot be opened right\nnow (each with its own code), **422** for what could never be paid online.\n\nThe Order handed back is always the one the charge **records**: it is recorded before this\nanswers, a reopen fetches it by its id, and an Order the call made that the charge does not\nrecord is never handed out (a 409 `checkout_in_progress` instead; the next request gets the\nrecorded one).",
        "operationId": "open_checkout_api_v1_payment_checkouts_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PlatformCheckoutIn"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PlatformCheckoutOut"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "The organization has no payable charge for this invoice."
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Refused, with a stable machine code in `errors[0].code`: `invoice_already_paid` (field `invoice_id`; the invoice is paid \u2014 the only 409 that means paid), `checkout_in_progress` (another request holds the checkout; try again in a moment), `previous_checkout_not_closable` (the expired checkout could not be closed yet; try again shortly), `previous_checkout_payment_in_flight` (a payment on a previous checkout is still being processed; try again in a few minutes), `checkout_not_supported` (the provider has no hosted checkout)."
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Could never be paid online, refused before any provider call, with `errors[0] = {field, code, message}`: `phone_required` (field `customer.phone`), `customer_details_required` (field `customer`), `currency_unsupported`, `amount_below_minimum` and `nothing_to_pay` (field `invoice_id`). A malformed body is a 422 with the framework's own field errors."
          }
        },
        "summary": "Open (or reopen) the checkout for an invoice",
        "tags": [
          "checkout"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/payment/checkouts/{charge_id}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Read-through status: while the checkout is open the provider is asked, server to server, what\nhappened to its Order, and the answer reconciled like a signed webhook's. What the return page\npolls. `paid` is true only for a captured payment. A checkout closed as `checkout_expired` is\nstill asked about inside its late-capture window: a payment made on its Order after it closed is\nrecorded, and the answer is `paid: true`.",
        "operationId": "get_checkout_api_v1_payment_checkouts__charge_id__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "charge_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "format": "uuid",
              "title": "Charge Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PlatformCheckoutStatusOut"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "The state of one checkout (asks the provider while it is open)",
        "tags": [
          "checkout"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/payment/checkouts/{charge_id}/confirm": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Razorpay's Checkout hands the browser `{payment_id, order_id, signature}`. This checks the\nsignature \u2014 `HMAC-SHA256(order_id|payment_id)` under the key secret, in constant time \u2014 and that\nthe Order is this checkout's; a missing field, a mismatch or a signature that is not the digest\nis a **400 and nothing is marked paid**. Only then does it ask Razorpay (`order_payments`) and\nreconcile the answer. The callback proves nothing: `paid` is true only if that answer shows a\ncaptured payment.",
        "operationId": "confirm_checkout_api_v1_payment_checkouts__charge_id__confirm_post",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "charge_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "format": "uuid",
              "title": "Charge Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CheckoutConfirmIn"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PlatformCheckoutStatusOut"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Razorpay: verify Checkout's callback signature, then ask Razorpay what happened",
        "tags": [
          "checkout"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/payment/collections/merchant-account": {
      "delete": {
        "operationId": "delete_merchant_account_api_v1_payment_collections_merchant_account_delete",
        "responses": {
          "204": {
            "description": "Successful Response"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Disconnect the organization's payment-provider account",
        "tags": [
          "collections"
        ]
